C - FUNCTIONS
==============

Reusable blocks of code.


BASIC FUNCTION
---------------
int add(int a, int b) {
    return a + b;
}

int main() {
    int result = add(5, 3);
    printf("%d\n", result);
}


SYNTAX
------
return_type name(parameters) {
    code
    return value;
}


RETURN TYPES
------------
int             Returns whole number
float           Returns decimal
char            Returns character
void            Returns nothing


PARAMETERS
----------
int add(int a, int b)

a and b are parameters.
You pass values when calling.


EXAMPLE
-------
void greet(char *name) {
    printf("Hello %s\n", name);
}

greet("Alice");


NO RETURN
---------
void printNumber(int x) {
    printf("Number: %d\n", x);
}

No return statement needed.


TIPS
----
Functions organize code.
Give clear names.
Keep functions small.
One job per function.
